---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Learn how Wellridge Partners approaches funding qualification, compliant proposals, and bounded program operations.">
  <section class="py-20 bg-gradient-to-b from-white to-fog">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-6">About Wellridge Partners</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold mb-6">Our Mission</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6">
        Wellridge Partners helps nonprofits and public-sector organizations move from a qualified funding opportunity to a compliant proposal—and, where the scope fits, into disciplined program launch and operations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-fog">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold mb-6">Our Philosophy</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6">
        <strong class="text-slate-deep">Strategy-first, structure always.</strong> The first question is whether the opportunity, buyer, budget path, timeline, capacity, and scope fit. When they do, clear narratives, evidence-backed budgets, compliance controls, and named owners make the work manageable.
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6">
        Our role can extend beyond submission into implementation planning, deliverable calendars, stakeholder coordination, reporting, records, and closeout. Every engagement is bounded by a statement of work; Wellridge does not guarantee awards or claim clinical or technical authority.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold mb-8">Our Approach</h2>
      <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold mb-3 text-ridge-blue">Rigor</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">
            We use scorecards, alignment matrices, and go/no-go reviews to surface eligibility, fit, dependencies, and reasons to pass before major effort begins.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold mb-3 text-ridge-blue">Clarity</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">
            Complex ideas deserve clear expression. We organize source material into traceable narratives, workplans, budgets, and compliance responses that are easier to review and approve.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold mb-3 text-ridge-blue">Momentum</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">
            Deadlines create stress, but structure creates calm. One source of truth, named owners, decision dates, and review gates keep work moving without relying on memory alone.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold mb-3 text-ridge-blue">Accountability</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">
            Each scope defines deliverables, inputs, roles, approvals, and acceptance. Where post-award work is included, the same discipline carries into launch, reporting, records, and closeout.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-fog">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold mb-6">About Felix</h2>
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-lg shadow-sm">
        <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 items-start">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0">
            <img
              src="/felix-torres.jpg"
              alt="Felix Torres"
              class="w-64 h-64 object-cover rounded-lg shadow-md"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4">
              Felix Torres leads Wellridge Partners. His background includes nonprofit operations, grant and federal-application workflows, reporting, education, public-facing programs, writing, and executive coordination.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4">
              His role centers on opportunity judgment, solution design, client interviews, narrative architecture, and final quality control. The delivery model pairs that judgment with explicit calendars, compliance matrices, evidence records, and named owners for routine follow-through.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-700">
              He shares practical notes on funding qualification, proposal structure, and program operations in the Wellridge Partners Insights library.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold mb-6">Scope Before Scale</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6">
        Wellridge accepts work only when it can own a defined work package and real deliverables. Legal, accounting, engineering, evaluation, or clinical judgment remains with appropriately qualified professionals named for that role; specialist capacity is never implied by the Wellridge brand alone.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-20 bg-slate-deep text-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-serif font-bold mb-6">Exploring a Bounded Scope?</h2>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 mb-8">
        Review the current service paths, then check the contact page for inquiry availability.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/contact"
        class="inline-block px-8 py-3 bg-ridge-blue text-white rounded-md text-lg font-medium hover:bg-opacity-90 transition-colors"
      >
        View Contact Status
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
